# Written by jnprofile-python when the project had no .worktreedisposable. The file is yours: change it as the project
# needs. just worktrees-prune reads it: the ignored files that these gitignore patterns name can be made again, so they
# do not keep a worktree. uv sync --locked makes .venv again, and the tools make their caches again. A package that
uv pip install added is not in uv.lock, so it does not come back: add it with uv add instead.
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/
